From: Matt
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a4xx: look up OCMEM on the GPU node (7.3 port of patches-612 0102)

The "sram" phandle is on the GPU node, but a4xx passes the DRM device's
parent (the display controller), so of_get_ocmem() never finds it and the
A430 runs without GMEM. Pass the GPU platform device instead.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c
@@ -660,7 +660,7 @@
 							     a4xx_registers;
 
 	/* if needed, allocate gmem: */
-	ret = adreno_gpu_ocmem_init(dev->dev, adreno_gpu,
+	ret = adreno_gpu_ocmem_init(&pdev->dev, adreno_gpu,
 				    &a4xx_gpu->ocmem);
 	if (ret)
 		goto fail;
